=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough investigation of the Kath2 lab found no fault. Every office device (office_pc, enquiry, exam_cell, tpo) on the 192.168.3.0/24 segment can successfully reach all other network segments: IT (192.168.1.0/24 via router0), CS (192.168.2.0/24 via router0), principle (192.168.4.0/24 via router1), servers (1.0.0.0/8 via router2), and internet (128.168.0.0/16 via router2), with zero packet loss in all tests. Router1, the office gateway at 192.168.3.1, has a complete routing table: all four directly connected prefixes are present along with RIP-learned routes to every remote subnet. RIP v2 is correctly configured on all three routers with all directly connected interfaces included in the routing process. Both of router1's RIP neighbors — router0 (10.10.0.1) and router2 (20.20.0.2) — are actively exchanging updates with zero error counts and last-update timestamps under 20 seconds. IP forwarding is enabled (ip_forward=1) on all routers, and no iptables rules exist to block forwarded traffic. The helpdesk ticket cannot be reproduced: the network is fully converged and all inter-segment paths are operational. The user's reported outage was either a transient convergence delay at lab startup (RIP takes up to 30 seconds to distribute routes after first boot) or a false alarm. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===